%N A344565 Triangle read by rows, for 0 <= k <= n: T(n, k) = binomial(n, k) * binomial(binomial(n + 3, 2), 2).
%H A344565 G. C. Greubel, <a href="/A344565/b344565.txt">Rows n = 0..50 of the triangle, flattened</a>
%F A344565 T(n, k) = (n + 4)! / (8 * k! * (n - k)!).
%F A344565 From _G. C. Greubel_, Nov 14 2026: (Start)
%F A344565 T(n, k) = 3*binomial(k+4, 4)*binomial(n+4, k+4).
%F A344565 T(n, k) = 3*binomial(n, k)*binomial(n+4, 4).
%F A344565 T(n, n-k) = T(n, k).
%F A344565 G.f.: 3/(1 - (1+y)*x)^5. (End)
%e A344565 Triangle begins:
%e A344565   [0]   3;
%e A344565   [1]  15,     15;
